Z||000000||falconhulk||08-17-2001||03:02 PM||||Are the fiero's and the firebirds bolt pattern the same?  I have rims and hoosiers for my firebird that I would like to use on the fiero if they are the same.  Also anyone know where to get the rubber pieces for under the hood that keeps it snug?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Songman||08-17-2001||03:11 PM||||No, Fieros and Firebirds are different bolt patterns. Do a search for wheels and you will see what factory wheels will fit a Fiero.<P>Fieros are 5x100mm.<P>Don't know about the rubber pieces. What pieces are you talking about? If you mean the two pieces that are attached to the bottom side of the hood, I think all they do is keep the sunroof from hopping around if you have it stored up there.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||falconhulk||08-17-2001||03:19 PM||||There are a couple pieces.  The reason i ask is when I hit bumps it seems like the hood shakes.  The pass. side of the hood does not lock like the drivers side......I assumed this was normal?  I was thinking these rubber pieces some of which are there and some are not kept the hood from bouncing.  BTW when I say bounce it is not really "bouncing"  its more a shake that produces a noise because its not held tight like the drivers side.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Primaris||08-17-2001||04:22 PM||||There should be to studs with rubber tops at both corners of the hood.  These studds can be adjusted up or down to stop the shaking you describe.<P>------------------<BR>Signatures are a waste of bandwidth!||||reg||1
