Z||000008||rigdonhome||08-18-2001||11:56 PM||||Hey, Cadaver!<P>Let ME get THIS straight.  You wasted bandwith to gripe about someone else wasting bandwidth?  Hmmm...  You do the math.  <P>Take your negativity elsewhere.  If you knew anything about bandwidth you would know that it's not only cheap, but the affects of a few sentences of text are insignificant when you consider the bandwidth it takes to run a bbs.  <BR>I'm new to the Fiero bbs, but others I belong to drop users for stuff like this.  I'm all for nipping this in the bud.  Is there a certain person that monitors each topic or is the whole bbs monoitored by one person?  Who do I email?<P>Hey, I forgot!  I know the question has already been answered, but No the Fierbird wheels won't fit the Fiero...  However, there are a lot of other vehicles, even non-GM products, out there whose wheels WILL fit the Fiero.  ebay is a great place to find stuff like that, and the guys there that sell wheels regularly will know right away which wheels will fit the Fiero.  I've seen some nice ones come through off of new Subaru's.<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black<BR>5 speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Cherry!<p>[This message has been edited by rigdonhome (edited 08-19-2001).]||||reg||3
