Z||000017||falconhulk||08-22-2001||09:04 AM||||Well I am not sure that its the hood anymore.  Did some adjustments and the noise is still there.  Since I drive I cannot pinpoint the cause.  I am pretty sure its not the hood anymore.  I thought it was coming from the Pass front but my wife thinks  it may be the rear after riding and sticking her head out the window.  It happens after going over a rough spot but only on the pass side.  if I go over it on the drivers side it makes no noise at all!  When I get time I will try to track it down....it sounds like something lose tapping something stationary.  Might not be a problem but I am a worrier......||||reg||1
Z||000018||b lo 0||08-22-2001||10:12 AM||||Wow!  Why is everyone so snippy lately?  It seems like every innocent thread gets people mad at each other!  To tell the truth, I wouldn't want to rip my Fiero apart to figure out something I could just as easily ask the knowledgeable members of the Forum.  Look at it this way-it's a compliment.  He would rather ask US, regular Fiero people, before he undergoes a project.  I'm flattered, how bout you?  Yes, Fiero wheels are 5x100mm with 5" backspacing.  I'm getting ready to put Sunfire 5-spokes on the GT.  Most GM front-drivers have wheels which will fit the Fiero.  Poke around at a junkyard.  Have fun with the Fiero!<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">       <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.vstoreauto.com.com" TARGET=_blank>Audio Imagery</A>, budget-priced car audio supplies from people like Monster Cable, Sony & more!||||reg||1
